! Floating-point diagnostic jb_af1c, routine F207B "LOAD DOUBLE --
! UNCHANGED REGISTERS" (docs/jb_af1c_floating-point.pdf p.90, octal
! 014510.00-014522.00): two sub-tests of the other half of LOAD
! DOUBLE's contract.
!
! F207A checked that DL clears accumulator bits 60-107. This checks
! the sentence right after it (Ref. Manual p.96): "Accumulator bits
! 108-127 remain unchanged." B1 fills BOTH accumulator halves with
! ones (C1111 at offsets 64 and 0), loads all-zeros with DL, and the
! low twenty bits must still be ones; B2 does the reverse -- both
! halves cleared, DL of all-ones, and they must still be zero. The
! listing's own comment names the field in right-half terms, "$R
! 44-63", which is accumulator bits 108-127: the twenty bits below the
! double-precision fraction, addressed here as CT0110 of 20 bits at
! accumulator offset 0.
!
! B2 is the one that bites in the obvious wrong direction (a DL that
! cleared the whole right half would pass B1 and fail nothing else in
! F207A, since A1/A2 only ever check bits 60-107 for zero); B1 catches
! a DL that wrote the whole right half from the operand.
!
! Substitutions (SSIP framework, real listed addresses): SERS (octal
! 1304) -> FAIL halt, SEN (octal 1310) -> scratch, PASS -> the
! routine's exit at 014522.00 (the listing's "B,$+1.", followed by
! B,F207B1 / SIC,SEN0+.32 / B,SSW). Constants from the pool p.176.
!
! Instructions: BD, B, C1111/C0000 at accumulator offsets 64 and 0,
! DL(U), CT0110 over a 20-bit field at offset 0, SIC, BRGZ.
! verify_fp_arith_f207b_listing.py checks every word bit-for-bit.
!
! Observed: passed on the model as it stood after F207A -- DL already
! kept the right half's low twenty bits, so this block confirms the
! rule rather than correcting it.

! -- SSIP framework substitutes --
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0

! -- constants (pool p.176) --

        SLC, (8)22005.0
FPK0    DD(BU,64,8), (8)0000000000000000000000
        SLC, (8)22006.0
FPK1    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1777777777777777777777

! -- code (verbatim, at the listing's addresses) --
        SLC, (8)14510.0
FLD1B   BD, $+.32   ! F207B1: $R 44-63, 1 S remain 1 S
        C1111(BU,64), FPK1, 64   ! preset the left half
        C1111(BU,64), FPK1   ! and the right half
        DL(U), FPK0
        CT0110(BU,20), FPK1   ! acc bits 108-127 untouched
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        B, $+.32   ! F207B2: $R 44-63, 0 S remain 0 S
        C0000(BU,64), FPK0, 64   ! preset the left half
        C0000(BU,64), FPK0   ! and the right half
        DL(U), FPK1
        CT0110(BU,20), FPK0   ! acc bits 108-127 untouched
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
PASS    BEW, $                  ! 014522.00: the routine's exit ("B,$+1.")
        END, FLD1B
